<title>FINLAND: Finnish June EU-harmonised CPI up 1.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Finnish June EU-harmonised CPI up 1.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index harmonised to European Union standards rose 1.1 percent year-on-year in June after a 0.9 percent rise in May, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>			     June 1997	May 1997	 June 1996</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			+1.1 pct	 +0.9 pct	+1.2 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		    +0.2 pct	 +0.3 pct	+0.9 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1996=100)   101.4	    101.2	   102.5</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices rose 1.2 percent year-on-year and 0.2 percent month-on-month in June, it said.</p>
<p>			     June 1997	May 1997	June 1996</p>
<p> Yr/yr			+1.2 pct	 +1.0 pct    +0.4 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		    +0.2 pct	 +0.2 pct    +0.0 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)   114.2	    114.0	  112.9</p>
<p>Six economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure was for a 1.1 percent rise year-on-year and a 0.1 percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
